<!--
	Stray Dogs (rescued), by Qux - Qux.stray.dogs - the living home of Spidercamp's Dog Pack.
	Nineteen of its twenty-seven breeds ship with no coat variation at all; the Japanese dogs,
	the collie and the doberman already have theirs and are left alone.

	Every coat here is a tint on the breed's own texture, never a texture of ours: an
	AlternateGraphic with a colour and no texPath keeps the original sprite and recolours it.
	The tint multiplies, so a coat can only ever be darker or warmer than the original, never
	lighter - which is why the original stays the most common one.

	THE PALETTE IS PURPLEYAM'S, MEASURED.

	Each value below is the mean colour of one of the coats purpleyam painted for
	Colorful Coats - Cats and Dogs!, divided by the mean colour of the sprite it was painted
	over, which is the tint that would have produced it. Nothing of theirs is shipped here;
	what is reused is the choice of colours, and it is theirs. _tools/Measure-Coats.ps1
	recomputes the whole table from the two mods on disk.

		ink       (102, 94, 90)     from PoodleC, purpleyam's black poodle
		blue      (111,124,166)     from GreatDaneA
		grey      (122,122,122)     from CatMunchkinA
		stone     (137,132,130)     from ChihuahuaA
		chocolate (138,113, 98)     from PoodleB
		coffee    (145,120,100)     from ChihuahuaB
		slate     (150,155,171)     from CatSomaliB
		ashblue   (155,174,176)     from CatSphynxA
		iceblue   (188,228,255)     from CatSomaliA
		silver    (192,192,192)     from CatBengalA
		mist      (195,206,208)     from CatSphynxB
		taupe     (221,197,170)     from CatPersianA
		oatmeal   (231,216,204)     from ShihTzuA
		fawn      (234,216,172)     from ChihuahuaC
		champagne (242,205,190)     from PoodleD
		apricot   (246,244,215)     from PoodleA
		ivory     (255,249,201)     from CatNorwegianA

	purpleyam painted 26 coats, shipped as 78 files - three rotations each. Seventeen of the
	26 are reachable this way, and they are the seventeen above. The other nine are true
	repaints, lighter than the sprite underneath or a pattern rather than a shade, and a
	multiply cannot reach them at all.

	Each operation is wrapped in a conditional that fires only when the breed has no
	alternateGraphics of its own, so an upstream mod that adds its own coats one day silently
	wins, and <success>Always</success> keeps the log quiet for players who run neither mod.
-->

<Patch>

	<!-- Afghan hound - cream and gold in life, and the silkiest coat in the pack. -->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName = "SCAfghanHound"]/alternateGraphics</xpath>
		<nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<success>Always</success>
			<xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName = "SCAfghanHound"]</xpath>
			<value>
				<alternateGraphicChance>0.6</alternateGraphicChance>
				<alternateGraphics>
					<li><color>(246,244,215)</color></li>
					<li><color>(234,216,172)</color></li>
					<li><color>(195,206,208)</color></li>
				</alternateGraphics>
			</value>
		</nomatch>
	</Operation>

